[{"order":1,"type":"heading","text":"Maximal Extractable Value (MEV): Flashbots, Bundles, Arbitrage, and Liquidations"},{"order":2,"type":"paragraph","text":"Maximal Extractable Value (MEV) refers to the maximum value that can be extracted from block production in excess of the standard block reward and gas fees by including, excluding, or changing the order of transactions within a block. Originally known as Miner Extractable Value, the term evolved post-Ethereum proof-of-stake transition to encompass validators, searchers, and builders."},{"order":3,"type":"subheading","text":"Understanding MEV Searchers and Builders"},{"order":4,"type":"paragraph","text":"The MEV supply chain consists of three main participants: Searchers, Builders, and Validators. Searchers run specialized algorithms to monitor the mempool for profitable opportunities like arbitrage and liquidations. Builders aggregate these transactions into optimal blocks to maximize validator payouts."},{"order":5,"type":"bullet_point","text":"Searchers: Bots or developers scanning the mempool for MEV opportunities."},{"order":6,"type":"bullet_point","text":"Builders: Entities that bundle transactions into valid blocks using MEV-Boost."},{"order":7,"type":"bullet_point","text":"Validators: Network participants who propose and attest to blocks, choosing the most profitable block provided by builders."},{"order":8,"type":"subheading","text":"Flashbots and Bundles"},{"order":9,"type":"paragraph","text":"Flashbots is a research and development organization that mitigates the negative externalities of MEV, such as priority gas auctions (PGAs) congesting the Ethereum network. Flashbots introduced the concept of 'Bundles', which allow searchers to group multiple transactions together and specify their exact execution order without broadcasting them to the public mempool."},{"order":10,"type":"code","text":"const { FlashbotsBundleProvider } = require("@flashbots/ethers-provider-bundle");

// Example of submitting a bundle to Flashbots Relay
const builderPromise = FlashbotsBundleProvider.create(
  provider,
  authSigner,
  "https://relay.flashbots.net",
  "mainnet"
);"},{"order":11,"type":"subheading","text":"Arbitrage Strategies"},{"order":12,"type":"paragraph","text":"DEX arbitrage occurs when the price of a token differs across decentralized exchanges like Uniswap and Sushiswap. Searchers construct atomic transactions that buy the token on the cheaper exchange and sell it on the more expensive one within the same block, ensuring risk-free profit."},{"order":13,"type":"subheading","text":"Liquidation Strategies"},{"order":14,"type":"paragraph","text":"Lending protocols like Aave and Compound require over-collateralized borrowing. When the value of collateral drops below a specific threshold, liquidators step in to repay a portion of the debt in exchange for the discounted collateral plus a liquidation bonus."},{"order":15,"type":"paragraph","text":"By mastering MEV extraction via Flashbots bundles, developers can protect network state integrity while capturing profitable arbitrage and liquidation opportunities securely."}]
